WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.420
The story of Han Solo has finally been told.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.790
From the illicit way he got his ship to the
accidental way he got his name, Solo: A Star

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.280
Wars Story has everything you've ever wanted
to know about the galaxy's most famous ruffian

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.389
with a heart of gold.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.130
The conclusion of Solo comes down to a whirl
of double-crosses, with secret agendas being

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.760
revealed, and hard-won loyalties being betrayed.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.560
Han comes out on top in the end, of course,
but things get a little dicey for him and

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.220
his friends before the credits roll.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.560
Tantalizing story threads are left dangling,
with some surprising appearances hinting at

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.570
more story to come.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.539
It's a lot to take in all at once.

00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:37.350
Luckily, we've got some tricks up our sleeve
to help even the scruffiest-looking nerf herder

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.480
make sense of it all.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.399
In short, you're all clear, kid - let's explain
the ending to this thing and go home.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:46.659
Trust no one
After accomplishing a time-and-space-bending

00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:50.739
escape through the dangerous Maelstrom, Han
and company make their way back to the yacht

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:53.129
headquarters of gangster Dryden Vos.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.929
Their goal is to deliver a supply of refined
coaxium to Vos, coaxium being a valuable fuel

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:01.070
source that can also serve as a powerful explosive.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.780
Before delivering the goods to Vos, Han and
friends make nice with the Marauder Enfys

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.870
Nest, who unmasks herself to reveal that she's
a teenage girl fighting on behalf of a nascent

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:10.890
rebellion.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.610
Coaxium powers the universe, and she's been
trying to acquire the coaxium for the Cloud

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.820
Riders anti-establishment goals.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.780
Something about the arrangement speaks to
Han's rebellious streak, so the smuggler hatches

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.640
a plan to let Nest keep the goods.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.860
But Han's plan experiences complications when
it's revealed that his partner Beckett has

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.060
been in league with Vos the whole time.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.920
After warning Han throughout the movie to
trust no one, he finally demonstrates why

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.640
with his ultimate betrayal, leaving with the
coaxium - and Chewbacca.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.280
There is another
After Han's clever plan devolves into a gunfight

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.500
that leaves Vos and his men done for, Han
goes off in search of Chewbacca, while Qi'ra

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.240
stays behind in Vos' yacht.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.210
Qi'ra hails a mysterious hooded figure.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.060
It turns out to be someone many Star Wars
fans figured they would never see in the movies

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.590
again: prequel villain Darth Maul, improbably
back from an early demise to head up the crime

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.090
organization Crimson Dawn.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:03.340
A lot has changed since the last time we saw
this devilish foe, who was literally cut in

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.530
half by Obi-Wan Kenobi at the end of The Phantom
Menace.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.340
Left in pieces at the bottom of a massive
pit, Maul survived through sheer force of

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.720
will - and later thrived with the help of
some powerful robot legs.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.100
This is a Maul that's older, angrier, and
more dangerous than ever before.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.870
When Maul orders Qi'ra to come visit him on
his home world of Dathomir, Qi'ra obliges,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.020
leaving Han and Chewbacca behind on the planet.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.819
More like Enfys Best

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:31.430
After Chewbacca and Han Solo reunite, the
kind-hearted bandits drag their quarry of

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.390
coaxium back to the camp of the Cloud-Riders,
and former foil Enfys Nest.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.900
Initially, the big reveal around Nest is that
this big bad space marauder is actually a

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.861
young girl, but the more interesting twist
occurs as it becomes clear she's one of the

00:02:43.861 --> 00:02:46.440
warriors who helps to spark the galactic rebellion.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.410
Her final parting words to Han indicate her
belief that he'll find the way to the rebellion

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.470
one day, too.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.630
Solo shows Han rebelling against the Empire
for selfish reasons, but the original trilogy

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.520
sees him becoming a rebel for the sake of
others, not just himself.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.430
Interestingly, Nest is so young that she could
conceivably still be alive in the time of

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.930
Episode 9, should Disney and Lucasfilm feel
like going there.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.210
As scary as Nest is for the first chunk of
Solo, she really doesn't get to do much once

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.959
she reveals her true colors.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.250
But it's a wide galaxy, and it's a big franchise.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:20.280
If she proves to be a fan-favorite, there's
plenty of room for her to pop up somewhere.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.940
Gimme the prize

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.411
After Han's crew is pared down to just him
and Chewbacca, the two make their way to a

00:03:25.411 --> 00:03:28.920
new planet to catch up with Lando, and tie
up one last loose end.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.810
Han greets Lando with a move that will look
familiar to fans of The Empire Strikes Back,

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.590
throwing him off with the threat of a punch
before yanking him gruffly into a warm embrace.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.880
While the gesture seemed to be a spontaneous
show of affection in its first appearance,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.290
here the move is deployed with purpose.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.489
While they're in close contact, Han deftly
picks Lando's pockets, or rather, his Taxi

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:51.330
Driver-style wrist holster, pilfering the
extra cards he used to cheat the first time

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.390
they played Sabacc.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.650
Han's dishonorable vengeance allows him to
finally win the Millennium Falcon in a card

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.940
game bet, becoming the ship's sole owner up
through the events of Return of the Jedi.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.960
Curiously, Han appears to take the Millennium
Falcon well after L3-37's mind has been uploaded

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.970
to the ship's interface, and there's no indication
that he ever unplugs her from the ship and

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.239
gives her back to Lando.

00:04:11.239 --> 00:04:12.920
The implications are haunting.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.269
Not only does Han cheat his way to liberating
Lando from his beloved ship (and home), he

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:20.070
also appears to steal his best friend along
with it.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.389
No wonder Lando turned him over to Darth Vader.

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:24.850
A very big gangster

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.230
In the final moments of the movie, Han and
Chewie prepare for a trip to Tatooine to meet

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:33.960
"a very big gangster" - and no gangster in
the galaxy seems to be bigger or more grotesque

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.960
than Jabba the Hutt.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.810
While we always like to see puppets in these
Star Wars movies, that Jabba puppet is a real

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:41.590
headache to operate if you want the character
to be mobile.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:45.590
Maybe in the next one - if there is a next
one - we'll see the space slug get off his

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.590
butt a little.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.880
After all, CGI's come a long way since '97.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.200
Thanks for watching!

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.160
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.260
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

